openCR 1.3.0 is now on CRAN <https://CRAN.R-project.org/package=openCR>. This release (the first on CRAN since 1.2.0 in May) fixes various bugs and adds minor new features (control over sample size for AIC, a summary method for openCR objects, detector-specific learned responses bk etc.).  Names of existing learned responses have been moved around (e.g., bsession now refers to a within-session effect; see openCR-vignette.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/openCR-vignette.pdf> for details). openCR-examples.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/openCR-examples.pdf> has been revised. For a list of changes see here <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/openCR%201.3.0%20NEWS.txt>.

